.Dd June 25, 2026
.Dt SLCAN 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm slcan
.Nd serial-line CAN network interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "options CAN"
.Pp
.Nm ifconfig Cm slcan Ns Ar N Cm create
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a CAN network interface whose frames are carried by a
userspace daemon rather than by a kernel hardware driver.
Each
.Nm Ns Ar N
interface is backed by the character device
.Pa /dev/slcan Ns Ar N :
frames transmitted by
.Xr can 4
sockets on the interface become readable on the character device, and frames
written to the character device are delivered to the sockets as received
frames.
It is the CAN analogue of
.Xr tun 4 ,
and is intended to be driven by
.Xr slcand 8 ,
which bridges it to a serial-line CAN
.Pq Dq slcan
adapter.
.Pp
A
.Nm
interface is created with
.Cm ifconfig slcan Ns Ar N Cm create ,
or implicitly by
.Xr slcand 8 .
The character device may be opened by a single process at a time.
Both classic and CAN FD frames are supported.
.Pp
A
.Nm
interface is not IP-capable and carries only CAN frames.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr can 4 ,
.Xr tun 4 ,
.Xr vcan 4 ,
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr slcand 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
